    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0655" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg567"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/1551: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Guggenheim</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-28T11:00:00-05:00">March 28, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. My telegram No. 21, March 23, 4 p.m. Mortgage moratorium bill passed by the
                    Senate last night and prompt approval by the House of Representatives is
                    expected. Opinion regarding measure is very mixed. Foreign banking interests are
                    naturally very much opposed to it.</p>
                <p>The Senate also passed a bill authorizing the President to arrange for a delay in
                    payments of amortization on Government debts both foreign and internal.<anchor
                        n="8" xml:id="d557-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Guggenheim</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d557-f1" n="8" xml:id="d557-f1-content">
                <p>The law, approved April 3, 1933, was published in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gaceta Oficial</hi>, April 4, 1933.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
